  "query_preview": "..\nSunny and warm weather is expected over the coming week. Warmer\ntemperatures 3 to 7 degrees above normal are expected to\ncontinue into today with a slight 'cooldown' as a low pressure\nsystem passes to the north of the area this weekend into early\nnext week. Outside of the temperature decrease, the main impact\nwith this system is the elevated winds. Surface southwest winds\nat 10-20 mph and gusts 25-30 mph begin to pick up late this \nmorning into early this evening. The strongest southwest winds \nare expected on Sunday at 20-30 mph with gusts 35-45 mph. The\ncombination of strong winds and dry conditions bring near\ncritical fire weather conditions this afternoon and again \nMonday afternoon and critical fire weather conditions Sunday\nlate morning into the early evening, with a Red Flag Warning in\neffect Sunday. These elevated winds have the potential to loft\nareas of blowing dust, particularly on Sunday. Dust-prone areas\nlike along Interstate 10 from San Simon to Willcox and from\nTucson to Eloy can see decreases in visibility due to areas of\nchannelized dust.\n\nOnce this system passes, there is general troughiness that will\nkeep high temperatures near or slightly below normal through the\nwork week.",
